\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For the fixed-boundary critical nearest-neighbor XY model in an admissible planar domain, does its normalized complex spin distribution converge along the entire mesh sequence in $H^{-3}_loc$ to the specified critical vertex field $V_*$? Require convergence of every finite collection of smooth compactly supported smearings, their conjugates, and all mixed nonnegative integer moments.

\subsection{Short English statement}
For the fixed-boundary critical nearest-neighbor XY model in an admissible planar domain, does its normalized complex spin distribution converge along the entire mesh sequence in $H^{-3}_loc$ to the specified critical vertex field $V_*$? Require convergence of every finite collection of smooth compactly supported smearings, their conjugates, and all mixed nonnegative integer moments.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
